{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YSwr2RwuPufPfXnMxxQWA8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! So the behavior differs:\n- No --invalid flag (default): does NOT print invalid value to stdout, exits 2 ← this is what `--invalid=abort` does\n- --invalid=fail: DOES print invalid value to stdout, exits 2\n- --invalid=warn: DOES print invalid value to stdout, exits 0\n- --invalid=ignore: DOES print invalid value to stdout, exits 0\n- --invalid=abort: does NOT print invalid value to stdout, exits 2\n\nSo the default behavior is actually `abort`, not `fail`! Let me verify:","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":41935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":324},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1906c47b-d50a-4d3d-b5b7-1f0ca9abf10d","uuid":"e0c72054-5a72-4514-88b6-c9f73dd873bf"}
