{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015hm8TyVyDUeETULvy8ZMSo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the modes are:\n- **abort** (default): Don't print invalid value to stdout, print error to stderr, exit 2\n- **fail**: Print invalid value to stdout, print warning to stderr, exit 2\n- **warn**: Print invalid value to stdout, print warning to stderr, exit 0\n- **ignore**: Print invalid value to stdout, no warning, exit 0\n\nThe current Go implementation matches the `abort` behavior (which is the default). Good.\n\nNow, the SRD R4.2 says: \"Must exit 2 when an invalid number is encountered (unless --invalid=ignore or --invalid=warn is set).\"\n\n\nI need to implement the three missing modes to match gnumfmt's behavior, since R4.2 only explicitly requires the default exit 2 behavior plus the ignore and warn variants.\n\nNow I'm working through the implementation details. The core challenge is that when an invalid value is encountered, I need to decide whether to print it to stdout before handling the error—this behavior differs across the four modes. For the token and line processing functions, I'll need to refactor the error handling to support printing the value first in certain modes, then either continuing or exiting based on which mode is active. I need to refactor the field processing functions so they don't bail out on the first error—instead, they should preserve the original field value and collect any errors to report later. This way, invalid fields get passed through unchanged while still tracking that something went wrong.\n\nNow I'm testing the actual behavior with the abort mode to see how field errors should be handled—specifically whether a parsing error in one field should prevent the entire line from being printed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens":42259,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":506},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1906c47b-d50a-4d3d-b5b7-1f0ca9abf10d","uuid":"828dfc3f-5373-4b0e-9e8b-8ae8176776b7"}
